/target
**/node_modules
seed/dist

# icp-cli splits this directory in two, and only half is disposable:
#
#   .icp/cache/  built wasms, local network state, local canister IDs — all
#                recreatable on the next deploy.
#   .icp/data/   canister ID mappings for CONNECTED networks, i.e. mainnet.
#                MUST be committed. Losing it is not merely inconvenient here:
#                vetKD derives the decryption key from the canister ID, so a
#                lost mapping that leads to deploying a replacement canister
#                makes every sealed secret permanently unreadable.
/.icp/cache/

# Never commit a key or a secret. `icp identity export` writes a PEM to stdout,
# and it is easy to redirect that into the repo by accident.
*.pem
.env
.env.*
